 "notes": [
  "LeRobot's denoising loop is `for step in range(num_steps)` with a Python float time (flow_matching/euler loop). openpi's is `while time >= -dt/2` on CUDA tensors, which forces a CPU-GPU sync per step \u2014 protocol \u00a72 describes the openpi behaviour; it does NOT apply to this implementation.",
  "Both prefill and denoise force _attn_implementation='eager' (modeling_pi0.py), so no SDPA/flash path is taken.",
  "predict_action_chunk is timed, not select_action: select_action serves 49 of every 50 calls from an action queue without running the model.",
  "copy.deepcopy(past_key_values) at lerobot/policies/pi0/modeling_pi0.py:919 clones the whole 15.04 MB prefix KV cache once per denoising step (5.68 ms, 10.4 % of a step) \u2014 measured in results/20260921_E3_pi0_eager_probe/.",
